However, an unforeseen phenomenon also entered the Covid Equation this week: the possibility of treatment.
A new drug has arrived in the Czech Republic, anti-Virotriotic molonupiravir, which reduces the risk of a severe course of the disease by a one-in-a-half hospitalization and it is possible to treat it at home.
And it should soon be supplemented by Pfizer's paxlovid, which of the results so far reports a success rate of even 85 per cent.
