How not to drown in a box tsunami
Are you going to unbuild the presents under the Christmas tree, and all of a sudden you're at home covered with boxes and fillers?
This "waste" is again used by e-shops that lack packaging materials.
Therefore, there was a map of stores that will welcome your used boxes.
And not just at Christmas.
All packaging materials are designed in such a way as to withstand re-manipulation.
Therefore, it is a pity to treat them as a disposable waste.
After an agreement, anyone can come to the participating store (a map of the KAMsNIM.cz project contains almost 150) cardboard boxes, plastic or paper fillers.
This will support small companies, reduce the amount of waste generated and also avoid crowded blue containers.
The stores themselves welcome the packaging, which is currently lacking on the market and also the saved money, as packaging cardboard has risen by 50 % over the last period.
In the eyes of eco-minded customers, I also strengthen my brand.
TIERRA VERDE, an eco-drug and eco-cosmetics makers, is one of such stores.
Boxes and refill materials are transported to Popůvdek u Brna by individuals who will accumulate at home, but we are also contacted by companies with which we have arranged regular collections of deferred cartons.
Everything will be used when packing shipments from our e-shop.
Thanks to individuals and companies, we form a more considerate world together.
Our desire is to preserve the resources and beauties of nature to future generations, says Petra Lopušníková from Tierra.
However, the application www.KAMSNIM.cz shows not only the collection points for packaging material.
It serves as a search engine if you need to get rid of anything (where to get sorted waste from the home, where to hand over expired medicines, tires, retired electricals, batteries, light sources, large-volume waste, etc.).
All garbage can thus end up in the right place, moreover reusable things will find their second home.
A total map of the project contains more than 100 000 such places.
“Finally, collection yards, re-use centers, containers for textiles, food banks, charitable shops, SWAPs and other places that help to find use for things that would otherwise unnecessarily become waste,” adds Miroslav Kubásek, one of the authors of an application from the Učiďme Česko association.
