More than 60 per cent of the electorate came to Saturday's elections for the councils of four municipalities
New councils on Saturday voted in the municipalities of Komňa in Uherské Hradiště, Lužice in the Most region, Nová Ves in the Liberec region and Rovná in the Pelhřimov region.
The number of councillors in these villages fell below the statutory number, or the elected councils have disintegrated.
A total of 28 seats was bid for 99 candidates on Saturday.
The average age of the newly elected representatives is 46.7 years.
The eldest of them is 69, the youngest 33 years old.
The elaboration of the results of the Saturday Election is symbolically concluding a rather demanding but successful year.
A number of new or re-elections for municipal councils have taken place and, above all, highly-folected elections to the Chamber of Deputies, the Vice-Chairwoman of the Czech Statistical Office Eva Krumpová said.
Recalculated that due to the covid-19 outbreak, elections were more cost-of-efficiency for equipment and personnel security.
In Komeň in Uherské Hradišt', the Association of Independent Candidates, which won 27.76 percent of the vote and two seats in the seven-member assembly, won Saturday's elections.
The STAN candidate received 24.84 percent of the vote, which also means winning two seats.
Citizens for Komňa also received two seats in the council, 18.52 percent of the electorate gave them their vote.
Jana Křižková, the mayor of the municipality, who is a Member of the Confidants, also joined the council.
Komňans – independent candidates – reached one mandate in the council.
75.48 percent of eligible electors went to the polls.
In the village of Rovná in the Pelhřimov region the association Pro Rovnou won.
It received 50.50 percent of the vote, which means four seats out of seven.
There were two more representatives from the Association of Independent Candidates 1 and one from the Association of Independent Candidates 2.
Voter turnout was 93.62 per cent.
Re-election in Lužice in the Most region was once again won by Lužice and Svinčice by Mayor Jindřich John.
It received 56.73 percent of the vote and, as well as in 2018, it has four mandates in the seven-member council.
The second place went to the municipality for the people, which scored 43.27 percent of the electorate, so she will have three representatives in the council.
76.7 percent of the electorate came to the polls.
Elections in Nová Ves in the Liberec region were won by the independent candidates Hope for Nová Ves ahead of the ANO Movement.
59.88 per cent of voters voted for an association of independent candidates, earning four seats in a seven-member municipal council.
ANO got 40.12 percent of the vote and strengthened against regular elections in 2018, won a more mandate and has three.
Voter turnout was 42.9 percent of voters.
The results of the Electoral Commission will discuss the results of the elections on Monday.
After that, they will be published in the Collection of Laws.
