New timetables have been in force in Prague since Sunday, they will mainly affect commupanitional connections
Travelers in the Prague Integrated Transport (PID) are expecting several changes since Sunday, which mainly concern commemorative connections.
There have been new lines, some of them have changed the route, and others, on the contrary, have ceased to exist.
Mladoboleslav region is newly involved in an integrated system.
Excavators from Ceske Budejovice have been stopped in the capital since Sunday in the Zahradní Město station.
In the suburban train transport will run S7 trains, which on the route from Beroun to Český Brod pass through the Prague main railway station on the route from Beroun to Český Brod.
In the recently commissioned station Praha-Zahradní Město will newly stop the R17 express train from České Budějovice and Benešov.
PID will now expand into other areas.
Among other things, buses will go to Světlá nad Sázavou, Blatna near Jesenice, Staré Splavy and Turnov.
Incorporate buses will be incorporated buses in the Mladá Boleslav region, including lines with an overlap in the Liberec and Hradec Králové regions.
When integrating, 77 lines will be abolished, 37 new ones will be deployed and the operation will be adjusted to 12 operating.
There will be a new bus line 405 coming from Zličín, which will go all the way to Žatce.
There will also be a new direct connection Prague – Kralovice u Rakovník, which replaces the canceled S53 train line.
They will be reinforced in the morning rush hour and on the weekend connections from Prague to Rakovník, when the express line number 404 will now run out.
Lines 400 and 410 operating in the Liberec region are newly included in the PID system.
They come from the Střížkov metro station, not from Nádraží Holešovice station.
Basing line 400 goes through Mělník, Duba and Česká Lípa to Nový Bor and selected connections continue to Rumburk or Cvikov.
Additional line 410 goes through Mělník and Dubou to Doks, Mimoň and Jablonné in Podještědí.
On the other hand, traffic on a dozen Central Bohemian local lines, including Mochov, Dobříš or Rožmitál pod Třemšínem is newly abolished or restricted.
All trains with departure from Prague at 02:30 a.m. are canceled.
Due to the modernization of the railway, long-term restrictions will continue on the lines Prague – Beroun, Prague – Lysá nad Labem and around Kolín.
Revenues await passengers in other places as well.
Buses are replaced by some canceled railway lines or the section on line 420 from Dobříš extends with continuity from Prague, where it is possible to use PID tickets up to Milevsko.
The changes have been changed by the lines 540 to 543 in the Nymburk region and the routes of some buses on the border of Central Bohemia and Hořovice in the Pilsen Region have been modified.
