Pre-Christmas Czech Republic is terrorized by Agent Tesla.
While data in October pointed to a slight decline in offensive campaigns, last month, as at the end of the year approaches, the attacks significantly intensified at the end of the year.
We saw a big campaign with Agent Tesla on November 18.
The attacks are aimed specifically at the Czech Republic.
For the time being, attackers' strategy remains the same.
An inflerated attachment in an e-mail is meant to attract the user with a name that refers to payments and financial transactions.
While last month it had a dangerous appendix in the name the word invoice, this time it was labeled as A Copy of Receipt Corrections for 11:2021...exe," Martin Jirkal of Eset said.
Spyware contains functions that scan Internet browsers and other programs, such as Microsoft Outlook, Mozilla Thunderbird or Yandex e-mail clients.
Harmful code actively searches for stored credentials, which it then sends to attackers.
The last strong campaign took place in the Czech Republic at mid-August-September-September, and with the upcoming holidays and at the end of the year, the activity of attackers is growing again.
Spyware Formbook also remained active in November.
Contrary to Agent Tesla, attackers in this case do not focus specifically on the Czech Republic, and security specialists interceded rather campaigns with a global reach in November.
Compared to the October data, Formbook weakened slightly in November, but it continues to face almost one-fifth of all detections.
The attacks took place continuously throughout the whole month with increased activity on November 3, 10 and 15.
The formbook most often contained a .exe-vorite attachment that was called REQUEST FOR SPECIFICIATION.
However, there is also the name of the receipt.
Attachment in Czech can then be much more dangerous for Czech users.
A Significant Declination and Submersion of the activity is recorded by Security Analyst on the Fareit program, which was worth 1.6 percent of the attacks and has had no major offensive campaign in the Czech Republic for the past few months.
